  "recordType": "rule-chapter",
  "ruleText": "CHAPTER Saf-C 1400 CARNIVAL-AMUSEMENT RULES (RSA 321-A:2)\n\nREVISION NOTE #1:\n\nDocument #5607, effective 4-2-93, adopted rules relative to bungee jumping. Document #5607 contains a new part numbered Saf-C 1410 and new and amended rules in Saf-C 1401. The insertion of the new rules in Saf-C 1401 required the renumbering editorially of most of the new and existing rules in Saf-C 1401. The text of the existing rules in Saf-C 1401 was not included in Document #5607, and therefore the effective dates for these existing rules remain unchanged by Document #5607.\n\nDocument #5445, effective 8-12-92, contained emergency rules relative to bungee jumping, but these emergency rules EXPIRED: 12-10-92. Document #5445 contained new and amended rules in Saf-C 1401 and a new part numbered Saf-C 1410.\n\nREVISION NOTE #2:\n\nDocument #10507, effective 1-21-14, adopted rules in Saf-C 1400 which had expired and readopted or readopted with amendments other existing rules in Saf-C 1400. Those rules with source notes which indicate that the rules or selected paragraphs had previously been filed under Document #8342, effective 4-28-05, and had expired 1-2-14, had provisions which had been subject to extension pursuant to RSA 541-A:14-a, I past their normal expiration date of 4-28-13. They had expired pursuant to RSA 541-A:14-a, II and III(a) because the rules had not been adopted by the Department of Safety within 30 days after the agency was allowed to adopt under RSA 541-A:14, I.\n\nREVISION NOTE #3:\n\nDocument #14139, effective 11-28-24, readopted or readopted with amendment all of the rules in Chapter Saf-C 1400. Amendments included the renumbering of various rules as indicated in the source notes. The reserved number Saf-C 1406.02 was deleted as an editorial change during the certification process pursuant to RSA 541-A:15, I. Document #14139 replaces all prior filings for rules affecting Chapter Saf-C 1400.\n\nThe former rule Saf-C 1406.02 had been titled “Requirements for Inspectors Acceptable to the Commissioner” and was repealed by Document #8145, INTERIM, effective 8-25-04. The prior filings before Document #8145 affecting the repealed Saf-C 1406.02 included the following documents:\n\n#2229, eff 12-31-82\n\n#2950, eff 1-3-85\n\n#4531, eff 1-1-89\n\n#5276, eff 11-20-91\n\n#5940, INTERIM, eff 1-1-95\n\n#5952, eff 1-24-95, EXPIRED: 1-24-03\n\n#7833, INTERIM, eff 2-22-03, EXPIRED: 8-21-03\n\n#8045, eff 2-20-04",
  "source": "https://github.com/GraniteState/adm-rules-data/blob/1c92d82e0f03a582ca5b7a578588edf38de2318e/raw/2026-11-15/state_agencies/saf-c1400.html"
